add('P165-0002','conditional application with external inputs','Proposition 3.4.2, Remark 2: algebraic versus holomorphic lifting','The stated lifting consequence uses algebraic local triviality, while the converse invokes algebraization of holomorphic vector bundles on a projective variety.','Separate the Zariski local-triviality test from existence of a holomorphic projective bundle, and cite an algebraization theorem for vector bundles with its proper/projective hypotheses. A rational section must be regular in the required neighborhood, or be translated to a suitable local-triviality criterion; it is not an automatic consequence of an arbitrary holomorphic trivialization.','GAGA|projective bundle|Brauer obstruction|local triviality')
